{"id":"SOCY230","title":"Sociological Social Psychology","department":"Sociology","level":"Undergrad","credits":"3","description":"Why do people do that? Sitting at the nexus of sociology and psychology, this course surveys the various ways in which sociologists have answered this question. We investigate individuals-for example, how they develop and understand themselves in relation to others, how they choose to present themselves to the world, and how they form thoughts and opinions. And we study larger units of analyses, from small groups to the broader society. Topics covered include socialization, identity formation, social influence, group processes, how social processes shape individual behavior, and how human behavior shapes society.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201801","sections":1,"seats":180,"openSeats":8,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Jenelle Clark"],"removed":false},{"term":"201808","sections":1,"seats":192,"openSeats":62,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Jeffrey Lucas"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":1,"seats":192,"openSeats":44,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Amanda Dewey"],"removed":false},{"term":"201912","sections":1,"seats":25,"openSeats":13,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Amanda Dewey"],"removed":false},{"term":"202001","sections":1,"seats":180,"openSeats":34,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Amanda Dewey"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":1,"seats":192,"openSeats":79,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Amanda Dewey"],"removed":false},{"term":"202012","sections":1,"seats":25,"openSeats":14,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Kelly Beavan"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":1,"seats":180,"openSeats":47,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Justin Maietta"],"removed":false},{"term":"202105","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":30,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Simone Durham"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":1,"seats":192,"openSeats":52,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["J